":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Critical Metals Corp. operates as a mining exploration and development company in Germany, Australia, Austria, and Greenland. The company explores for lithium and rare earth element deposits. Its flagship project is the Tanbreez Project located in the Kujalleq region of southern Greenland. The company is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Antony William-Paul Sage B.Bus, B.Com., C.A., FCPA, FTIA | Executive Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 65","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5 people.","financial_summary":["Critical Metals Corp. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $871M market cap.","Returns on capital run at -47% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $14M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -21.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -110.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 2.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 48% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (31.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Basic Materials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 211% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Critical Metals (NASDAQ:CRML) Stock: Insider Sergey Savchenko Sells 66,667 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/critical-metals-nasdaqcrml-stock-insider-sergey-savchenko-sells-66667-shares.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793959758.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Metals Finalizes Acquisition of European Lithium, Issues Over 90 Million Shares on November 5, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/critical-metals-finalizes-acquisition-of-european-lithium-issues-over-90-million-shares-on-november-5-2026","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793889055.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.026,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Critical Metals Corp. Completes Acquisition of European Lithium","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/critical-metals-corp-completes-acquisition-140000476